00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.149 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  we are hearing from the mother of  two-year-old  amari nicholson for the first time since  her boyfriend was  arrested for amari's murder taylor  nicholson has stayed out of the public  eye since her son's body was found this  week  and it's a story many of you have been  following the i-team's vanessa murphy  first broke news of what many feared  police saying the child was murdered  tonight vanessa brings us her interview  with taylor nicholson  the gum is it yummy this is amari  nicholson  he was an innocent soul the  two-year-old's life was cut  short he was always a happy baby metro  police say terrell rhodes admitted to  beating omaree to death  on may 5th this man betrayed me  he hurt me amari's mother taylor  nicholson tells the i-team she showed up  in court friday to follow her now  ex-boyfriend's criminal case  rhodes faces charges including murder on  may 5  rhodes lied to police and said a woman  took amari from their place at the  emerald suites near paradise and twain  while nicholson was out of town the  couple then talked with eight news now  and rhodes shared a similar story what's  really sickening is that people  is making assumptions thinking that  i have something to do with it that i  have heard  manipulated in some way the las vegas  community jumped into action to search  for amari  whatever it takes to bring omaree home  we're just pleading for the public's  help because we don't have any new  information  but four days after that interview with  eight news now  detectives say rhodes confessed to  killing omaree and hiding his body  on wednesday the toddler's remains were  found  my head just fell i was  disappointed i felt betrayed i just felt  my whole insides just fall out the  i-team has learned  one complaint was made to child  protective services alleging neglect  last  june but the allegations were found to  be unsubstantiated and the case was  closed  now on social media nicholson has  received criticism  people raising questions about whether  she had any involvement or knowledge  about amari's death  and at this vigil wednesday night an  event to remember amari turned  to harsh words for the mother you need  to feel the pain at each and every one  of those people standing here today  taylor nicholson says she feels like  public enemy number one  she understands members of the public  are suspicious of her  but she insists she's just a grieving  mother  i can't grieve in peace i can't grieve  properly at all  i'm being advised to stay home because  it's unsafe  i'm the one hurting the most my baby's  gone  i can't it's hard  she declined to say why she left amari  with rhodes while she was in colorado to  help her mother  but she insists she had no knowledge of  what happened to amari  did you believe tyrell when he said a  woman  came to pick up amari i did  i i had trust in him  and i would have never fathomed  that this would have been the outcome  was there ever a point before his arrest  where you didn't believe him  no not necessarily didn't believe  just started being more aware of  the signs until  on wednesday when we went to metro clark  county district attorney steve wolfson  says investigators have found no  evidence to believe  nicholson committed a crime you don't  believe that she knew  or was lying at this point the  information that's been provided to me  by the authorities is that she didn't  lie  and that although some may question some  of the decisions and judgments she made  that it doesn't rise to the level of  criminal behavior nicholson says she's  planning private arrangements to mourn  the loss of her son  you still see him running around you  still see everything you still hear  everything  and now we just gotta live through what  he loves the most  to keep his spirit close to all of us  and  until then one time we could see him  again  vanessa murphy 8 news now  vanessa also asked the clark county d.a  whether he will seek the death penalty  against terrell rhodes he says it's too  early to know right now he says his  office  is considering attempted murder charges  against rhodes  after police say he fought with police  officers and grabbed an officer's gun  you can watch vanessa's full interview  with amari's mother  at 8newsnow.com

